WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.810
The COO is the role of someone who
needs to be a jack of many trades and

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.140
a master of many trades.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.780
That's a complex role.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:14.670
It's someone who can drive operational
excellence, but also be able to understand

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:19.428
trends, create systems, put researchers
together to drive innovation.

00:00:19.428 --> 00:00:25.190
The Emerging COO: Driving Innovation and
Operational Excellence, is a program for

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:29.740
current or aspiring CEO's,
is a program that

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:34.730
provides CEOs with frameworks to
help them become more effective and

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:38.940
successful in this complicated and
multifaceted process.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.750
&gt;&gt; There's very few programs purposely for
COOs.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:47.700
I was really looking for a hybrid between
the operations and the innovation so,

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.710
go figure,
that's exactly what this is tailored for.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:57.050
&gt;&gt; To come together with a cohort who
really are facing similar challenges,

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:00.430
that community building is such
a big part of the program.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:05.990
&gt;&gt; It's just so fun to hear about people's
challenges which are very similar,

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:08.060
I think across the board,
no matter the industry.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.920
&gt;&gt; We have manufacturing companies here.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.660
We have nonprofits here.

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:13.610
We have technology companies here.

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:17.530
And we were able to take all the data and
connect it to all of our organizations.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:21.250
&gt;&gt; There's no recipe of what a CEO does.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:22.170
Depends on where you are,

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:27.020
what you do and having that sounding
board in that role is really therapeutic.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.970
&gt;&gt; We find that by bringing people
from different industries and

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:34.790
different stages,
we actually generate better ideas.

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:38.440
Being in the heart of Silicon Valley,
its exposure to really

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:42.450
the most innovative companies not
just innovative in technology,

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:47.500
but, innovative in organizational
practices, employee engagement,

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:51.060
how to scale,
how to grow quickly is really powerful.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:56.260
&gt;&gt; Something that is unique is this
three month blended experience

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:00.700
that is broadcasting to three modules we
utilize a combination of online learning,

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:04.970
face to face learning, and experiential
learning at your organization.

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:09.090
&gt;&gt; Being able to practice and use some
of the concepts in a real life work

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:14.440
project is the key to actually getting
the most out of an experience like this.

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:18.876
&gt;&gt; A lot of what we teach and frameworks
that we share, arm you with tools and

00:02:18.876 --> 00:02:22.688
a healthy dose of confidence that
you can take on the unknown.

00:02:22.688 --> 00:02:25.006
&gt;&gt; I'm already thinking differently.

00:02:25.006 --> 00:02:28.350
There's already concepts that I need to
share with the team that are either new or

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.720
things that are old but
they've been refreshed from being here.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.450
&gt;&gt; The knowledge that I'm taking back
from this program will give the company

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:36.220
a huge advantage.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.730
And to think outside of the box.

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:41.977
&gt;&gt; I think I had high expectations for
a Stanford educational program like this,

00:02:41.977 --> 00:02:44.628
but it's exceeded my expectations,
for sure.

00:02:44.628 --> 00:02:45.514
[MUSIC]

00:02:45.514 --> 00:02:49.981
&gt;&gt; COOs are often times they
are unrecognized heroes in the senior

00:02:49.981 --> 00:02:52.600
leadership seat of organizations.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:57.220
They are the builders, the ones that
work quietly behind the scenes to make

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:03.659
the organization work and this is a very
optimistic place with a can do attitude.

00:03:03.659 --> 00:03:07.341
COOs, we find it hard,
not to experience that.

